 getting in  our store but when you do find one whose  fault is it and so if there is one we'll  make sure the customer is made whole on  that product and we're gonna work with  the customer or work with brands to go  after that bad actor on average 95  percent of the time we investigate that  and take action within eight hours  inventor mark Lowe pre ATO says that  wasn't the case  for his business the forearm forklift  lifting straps make your forearms a  fulcrum after listing his forearm  forklift on Amazon he says he found  dozens of fakes some using the same name  logo and photos this is my wife this is  me lo pre Otto says it's not only  extremely difficult to track down the  bad actors but also to take any legal  recourse against them we have to find  them deep in their website then report  them still more and more days are  passing and then finally they may or may  not take down the listing amazon filed  suit against a few sellers who were  counterfeiting low Prieto's product and  160 thousand dollars in may 2000 18 that  money went to low pre auto we really  want to go as fast as we can but now  meta says amazon wants to make it easier  to remove fakes by teaming up with  sellers in a new program called project  zero this is the first time we've given  brands the ability to directly remove  stuff from our store let's pretend  you're a brand who's in project zero he  showed us how approved sellers can now  identify and delete suspected  counterfeit listings with just a few  clicks you're given them a lot of  responsibility we are giving brands a  lot of responsibility we will always  have some level of vetting there's some  powerful tools in there and you wouldn't  want some random person showing up and  starting to remove products from our  store the company says part of that  vetting process is keeping the program  by invite only 500 brands are currently  participating but meta says that number  will grow significantly Amazon is also  using artificial intelligence to search  for fakes and offering sellers an option  to add a special code to each product  that buyers can scan with Amazon's app  to make sure it's real Bob Barr kc with  the international anti counterfeiting  coalition says consumers need to be  aware of what he calls the three P's  price point of sale and packaging if  it's too good to be true  it's probably fake packaging  misspellings specifically for Amazon you  also may want to look at the customer  reviews that it was a verified purchaser  you really think that's gonna make the  difference here I don't think that will  make the difference on its own  so when I look at project zero it really  is the combination of all the automation  all the machine learning and everything  we can do up front the success the  growth of Amazon is all built on having  to have customers trust us small medium  businesses and brands trust us because  that's the only way we're gonna thrive  for CBS this morning Carter Evans  Seattle I'm glad they're addressing it  you know as someone who orders a lot of  stuff from Amazon I don't want fake  products that could be dangerous and  also you when you hear them talk about  it it sounds vague and then when you see  they've given product makers the power  to delete others that's pretty that's a  lot of power again we'll see if that  works out we're paying attention
 

